    "core:description": "Synthetic paging channel, one full cycle (15.95 s) of the paging test signal: POCSAG 512, 1200, 2400 bit/s (4.5 kHz deviation) and one FLEX frame each at 1600/2, 3200/2, 3200/4, 6400/4 (4.8 kHz deviation), 0.5 s of silence after each transmission. The channel (466.075 MHz) is 50 kHz below the centre; the carrier is 700 Hz above it. Carrier-to-noise 20 dB in 25 kHz. At 192 ksps it is the rate a whole-span carrier bank hands a pager receiver (the wide-input setting). See specs/trunk.md section 8.",
